# Packages the repository carries that are not ours (NOT_OURS in apt/make-only-ours.py): another archive's package,
# only repackaged or rebuilt through Lean Code, which that archive keeps updating. Its builds are not blocked, and ours ranks
# under them, so the newer one from that archive wins; ours is only the way in.
#   deb-multimedia-keyring: deb-multimedia's own keyring, 2024.9.1 in deb-multimedia (2024.9.1+lc1 here). The repository carries it so that sparky-stereo-apt can depend on it before deb-multimedia is in the sources; when deb-multimedia rotates its key, its new keyring package must reach the edition, or the edition's deb-multimedia source breaks.
#   libunibreak-dev: Debian's libunibreak 7.0-2, as libunibreak7; Debian's libunibreak-dev 8.0-2 must not be blocked or outranked.
#   libunibreak-doc: Debian's libunibreak 7.0-2, as libunibreak7; Debian's libunibreak-doc 8.0-2 must not be blocked or outranked.
#   libunibreak7: Debian's libunibreak 7.0-2, rebuilt only through Lean Code, carried when Debian testing moved to libunibreak8 on 2026-10-16 while deb-multimedia's libass9 still needed libunibreak7; Debian's source is at 8.0-2 now (and deb-multimedia's libass9 2:0.17.5-dmo3 needs libunibreak8).
#   libunibreak7-dbgsym: the debug symbols of the carried libunibreak7 (Debian's are in its debug archive).
Package: deb-multimedia-keyring:any libunibreak-dev:any libunibreak-doc:any libunibreak7:any libunibreak7-dbgsym:any
